@startuml
' ResumeGPT — user story: "user creates a project and it persists"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

title Create project and persist it

actor User as U
participant "React UI\n(Projects view + modal)" as UI
participant "API server\n(POST /api/projects)" as API
participant "Prisma\ndata-access" as ORM
database "SQLite\n(dev.db)" as SQL

U -> UI : open "Add project" modal
U -> UI : fill title, description,\ncourse, skills; submit
activate UI

UI -> UI : validate title & description non-empty

alt validation fails
  UI --> U : inline error\n"Add a project title and description to continue."
  note right of UI : no HTTP request is sent;\nentered values stay in the form
else input is valid
  UI -> API : POST /api/projects\n{title, course, semester, description,\nskills, source}
  activate API

  API -> API : validate payload, parse\nskills CSV into array

  alt payload rejected (400)
    API --> UI : 400 {error}
    UI --> U : show error, keep form open
  else payload accepted
    API -> ORM : project.create({ data: { ..., userId } })
    activate ORM
    ORM -> SQL : INSERT INTO Project
    activate SQL
    SQL --> ORM : new row (id, createdAt)
    deactivate SQL
    ORM --> API : Project record
    deactivate ORM
    API --> UI : 201 { project }
    UI -> UI : prepend project to list
    UI --> U : close modal, show\n"Project added to your library."
  end

  deactivate API
end

deactivate UI

note over API, SQL
  Target architecture. The current build still
  writes to localStorage; the API + Prisma layers
  land with issue #8.
end note

@enduml
